-- title:
--   Leibniz rule for the slab pairing along an archimedean direction
-- statement:
--   Fix a character $\omega$ of the idele units of $\mathbb{Q}$ with values in $\mathbb{C}^\times$, all of whose values have absolute value $1$, real numbers $a,b$, and a set $\Phi_0 \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ with `IsSlabDomain a b Φ₀`, i.e. $0 < a < b$ and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the range of `globalPointsGL 3 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ` with respect to the adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_3$ restricted to the locus `ideleNormDetSlab a b`; the measure used below, `domainMeasure a b Φ₀`, is that slab measure further restricted to $\Phi_0$. Assume the Siegel-type hypothesis `hW0a`: there are $c > 0$ and $C$ such that every $g$ admits $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$ and $n,t,k$ with $\gamma g = ntk$, where $n$ and $t$ are trivial at every finite place, $k$ lies in `localMaximalCompact3` at every finite place, and at each infinite place $n$ is upper unipotent with all entries of norm at most $C$, $t$ is diagonal with `archRoot₁` and `archRoot₂` at least $c$, and $k$ is orthogonal. Let $u : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}) \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous, invariant under left translation by global points, satisfying $u(zg) = \omega(z)u(g)$ for central adelic scalars $z$, of moderate growth in the sense that $\|u(g)\| \le C' \,\mathrm{gauge3}(g)^N$ for some $C', N$, and cuspidal along both `radicalP21` and `radicalP12` in the sense that for every $g$ the iterated integral of $u$ over the two-parameter radical vanishes, the integrations being against the adelic additive Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box. Let $\varphi, \varphi'$ be smoothing kernels, that is, each is a product of a smooth compactly supported archimedean factor supported away from the vanishing of the determinant with the indicator of a family of open compact subgroups at the finite places agreeing with `localMaximalCompact3` for all but finitely many primes. Then for any indices $i,j \in \{0,1,2\}$ the function $$s \mapsto \int_{\Phi_0} (\varphi * u)\big(g\,L(I + sE_{ij})\big)\,\overline{(\varphi' * u)\big(g\,L(I + sE_{ij})\big)}\,d\mu(g),$$ where $L$ is [`WhittakerBlock.archRealLift3`](def/LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_ArchSmooth3.html#L18) and $\varphi * u$ denotes `smoothingOperator`, has derivative at $s = 0$ equal to $$\int_{\Phi_0} \partial_{ij}(\varphi * u)\cdot \overline{\varphi' * u}\,d\mu \;+\; \int_{\Phi_0} (\varphi * u)\cdot \overline{\partial_{ij}(\varphi' * u)}\,d\mu,$$ with $\partial_{ij}$ the archimedean derivative `WhittakerBlock.archDeriv i j`.
--
--   This is the differentiation-under-the-integral step behind the $\mathfrak{g}$-antisymmetry of the slab pairing of two smoothed cusp forms: the Leibniz rule for the Petersson-type pairing over the slab fundamental domain along the one-parameter archimedean subgroup generated by $E_{ij}$. It is used, together with the invariance of the pairing under right archimedean translation, by `integral_archDeriv_smoothingOperator_mul_conj_eq_neg`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_SlabL2_hasDerivAt_integral_smoothingOperator_comp_archRealLift3_mul_conj.lean

